Right: a triangulation of $X'$.}
\label{fig_nc_lem_c_triang}
\end{figure}

\begin{lemma}\label{lem_both_inside}
Let $\Delta$ be the triangle of Lemma~\ref{lem_c_triang}.
Any segment of $S$ that has a non-empty intersection with the interior of
$\Delta$ either has both its endpoints inside $C_{a,b,\beta}$ or crosses $t$;
in the latter case the endpoint that is inside $R_{a,b,\beta}$ is also
inside $C_{a,b,\beta}$.
\end{lemma}

