The rejection package is now complete. The generator is preserved as required, G1–G8 still pass after the final edits, and `selftest_report.json` records G9 as failed rather than claiming success. I also preserved the hard bare and hard hinted script-owned transcripts; no placebo result was fabricated after the gated failure instructed us to stop. Temporary scratch copies were moved out of the result directory to `/tmp/1211.1490-scratch.5e6o5v`; the canonical rejected module remains in place.
The family passed construction/verification/local-hardness gates but failed the mandatory hinted-oracle gate at both the original shipping rung and the single permitted higher rung. Per the task, it is preserved and documented as rejected rather than tuned further.
  ✓ Validate the paper’s exact reduction, easy regimes, and certificate route; choose track/family
  ✓ Implement the deterministic generator, exact verifier, parser, attacks, and self-tests
  ✓ Run and repair all local gates; benchmark shipping costs and write selftest report
  ✓ Run the bare and G9 oracle hardening arms, then set the shipping preset or reject honestly
  ✓ Write the rejection report and preserve the implementation/evidence
