codex
Rejected honestly under Track B: the family passed G1–G8, but failed mandatory G9(b). The structural hint enabled a verified oracle solution at both \(n=77\) and the one permitted escalation, \(n=89\).

Key evidence:

- Random guessing: 0/200,000; exact density \(2^{-89}\).
- Four adversarial attacks: all 0/8.
- Reference Gaussian elimination: median 15,039 XORs.
- Compact route: at most 291 XORs.
- Hard bare arm: 0/3 counted solves.
- Hard hinted arm: 1/3 solved and verified exactly.

Files:

- [REJECTED.md](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1211.1490/REJECTED.md)
- [Preserved generator](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1211.1490/rejected_gen_1211_1490.py)
- [Self-test report](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1211.1490/selftest_report.json)
- [Bare transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1211.1490/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)
- [Hinted transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1211.1490/g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl)

No placebo run was fabricated after G9(b) instructed rejection and termination. The construction is based on [Section 5 and Appendix A of the paper](https://arxiv.org/abs/1211.1490).
